fragment_downloaded_cb({"url":"base/gstadapter.html#gst_adapter_take_buffer","fragment":"\n\tgst_adapter_take_buffer\n\n\n\tGstBase.Adapter.prototype.take_buffer\n\n\n\tGstBase.Adapter.take_buffer\n\nReturns a GstBuffer containing the first nbytes bytes of the\nadapter. The returned bytes will be flushed from the adapter.\nThis function is potentially more performant than\ngst_adapter_take since it can reuse the memory in pushed buffers\nby subbuffering or merging. This function will always return a\nbuffer with a single memory region.\nNote that no assumptions should be made as to whether certain buffer\nflags such as the DISCONT flag are set on the returned buffer, or not.\nThe caller needs to explicitly set or unset flags that should be set or\nunset.\nLikewise, no assumptions should be made about timestamps and offset of the\nreturned buffer. The caller should use gst_adapter_prev_pts,\ngst_adapter_prev_dts, and gst_adapter_prev_offset to obtain the relevant\ninformation.\nThe returned buffer might not be writable, use gst_buffer_make_writable\nif you need to change e.g. flags or timestamps.\nSince 1.6 this will also copy over all GstMeta of the input buffers except\nfor meta with the GST_META_FLAG_POOLED flag or with the \"memory\" tag.\nCaller owns a reference to the returned buffer. gst_buffer_unref after\nusage.\nFree-function: gst_buffer_unref\nParameters:\na GstAdapter\nthe number of bytes to take\na GstBuffer containing the first\nnbytes of the adapter, or NULL if nbytes bytes are not available.\ngst_buffer_unref when no longer needed.\nReturns a Gst.Buffer containing the first nbytes bytes of the\nadapter. The returned bytes will be flushed from the adapter.\nThis function is potentially more performant than\nGstBase.Adapter.prototype.take since it can reuse the memory in pushed buffers\nby subbuffering or merging. This function will always return a\nbuffer with a single memory region.\nNote that no assumptions should be made as to whether certain buffer\nflags such as the DISCONT flag are set on the returned buffer, or not.\nThe caller needs to explicitly set or unset flags that should be set or\nunset.\nLikewise, no assumptions should be made about timestamps and offset of the\nreturned buffer. The caller should use GstBase.Adapter.prototype.prev_pts,\nGstBase.Adapter.prototype.prev_dts, and GstBase.Adapter.prototype.prev_offset to obtain the relevant\ninformation.\nThe returned buffer might not be writable, use gst_buffer_make_writable (not introspectable)\nif you need to change e.g. flags or timestamps.\nSince 1.6 this will also copy over all GstMeta of the input buffers except\nfor meta with the Gst.MetaFlags.POOLED flag or with the \"memory\" tag.\nCaller owns a reference to the returned buffer. gst_buffer_unref (not introspectable) after\nusage.\nFree-function: gst_buffer_unref\nParameters:\na GstBase.Adapter\nthe number of bytes to take\na Gst.Buffer containing the first\nnbytes of the adapter, or null if nbytes bytes are not available.\ngst_buffer_unref (not introspectable) when no longer needed.\nReturns a Gst.Buffer containing the first nbytes bytes of the\nadapter. The returned bytes will be flushed from the adapter.\nThis function is potentially more performant than\nGstBase.Adapter.take since it can reuse the memory in pushed buffers\nby subbuffering or merging. This function will always return a\nbuffer with a single memory region.\nNote that no assumptions should be made as to whether certain buffer\nflags such as the DISCONT flag are set on the returned buffer, or not.\nThe caller needs to explicitly set or unset flags that should be set or\nunset.\nLikewise, no assumptions should be made about timestamps and offset of the\nreturned buffer. The caller should use GstBase.Adapter.prev_pts,\nGstBase.Adapter.prev_dts, and GstBase.Adapter.prev_offset to obtain the relevant\ninformation.\nThe returned buffer might not be writable, use gst_buffer_make_writable (not introspectable)\nif you need to change e.g. flags or timestamps.\nSince 1.6 this will also copy over all GstMeta of the input buffers except\nfor meta with the Gst.MetaFlags.POOLED flag or with the \"memory\" tag.\nCaller owns a reference to the returned buffer. gst_buffer_unref (not introspectable) after\nusage.\nFree-function: gst_buffer_unref\nParameters:\na GstBase.Adapter\nthe number of bytes to take\na Gst.Buffer containing the first\nnbytes of the adapter, or None if nbytes bytes are not available.\ngst_buffer_unref (not introspectable) when no longer needed.\n"});